The Divine Sense is a part of counsciousness split off from the cultivator's soul. It can be used to scan things or people (this is how cultivators check each other's cultivation level), to control artifacts (magic objects) or just to attack someone else directly. The Divine Sense can be spread out over an area with low precision or it can be focused on a specific point for more accuracy.

Sect Leader Huanglong burned his lifespan to become stronger in the fight. What does it mean ? Aren't Immortals immortal ?
No, they aren't immortal. The lifespan of a cultivator is a ressource that is finite and can be used in desperate situations (most cultivators keep their lifespan to live through it though). Lifespan is increased upon a breakthrough or consuming certain medecines (pills). You can think of cultivation as a game of cat and mouse between the cultivators (that cultivate and increase their lifespan) and the law of the heavens (that is coming after them if they run out of lifespan).

Pills are quite self-explanatory, they are medecines made from ingredients rich in spiritual energy and can have many different types of properties and usages. Pill-making is a form of external alchemy which is opposed to internal alchemy (cultivation).

The yellow paper Sun Dazhu was using to make a formation is called a talisman. Talismans have effects in function of what symbol is drawn on them, for example a speed talisman can be put on your legs in order to run faster. Talismans are pretty weak and overall only used by low level cultivators.

